var tid = ctx.Args["ETS.InterfaceTransactionID"].ToString().AsInt();
var trans = ctx.Api.Data.DbInterfaceTransaction.Load.ByID(tid);
var po = ctx.Api.Connect.Payloads.JsonpojsonPayloadToModel(trans.MessagePayload,tid).Return;

trans.EntityID = po.DataArea.OrderRequestHeader.ID;
trans.EntityKey = po.DataArea.OrderRequestHeader.BatchNumber;

// JOB CREATE BUSINESS LOGIC
var job = new ETS.Core.Api.Models.Data.DbJobDiscreteComposite();

job.Name = po.DataArea.OrderRequestHeader.BatchNumber;
job.ExternalID = po.DataArea.OrderRequestHeader.BatchNumber;
job.Description = po.ApplicationArea.Sender 
	+ " >>> " 
	+ po.ApplicationArea.Receiver 
	+ ": " 
	+ po.DataArea.OrderRequestHeader.Quantity 
	+ " Units of " 
	+ po.DataArea.OrderRequestHeader.Product;
      
var parsCustReqDate = DateTime.Parse(po.DataArea.OrderRequestHeader.CustomerRequestDate);
job.PlannedStartDateTime = parsCustReqDate;

job.Capture01 = ctx.Args["ETS.InterfaceTransactionID"].ToString(); //InterfaceTransactionID
job.Capture02 = po.DataArea.OrderRequestHeader.Product; //Product
job.Capture03 = po.DataArea.OrderRequestHeader.Quantity.ToVariantString(); //Quantity

var result = ctx.Api.Data.DbJobDiscreteComposite.Save.InsertAsNew(job).ThrowIfFailed();

trans.EndDateTime = ctx.Api.Util.DateAndTime.GetCurrentDateTimeForSiteID(1);

ctx.Api.Data.DbInterfaceTransaction.Save.UpdateExisting(trans).ThrowIfFailed();

## Slide 15

Interface Definitions

## Slide 16

Overview

Interface Definitions

Interface Definitions are defined as the pipe, or the way TrakSYS will transmit or receive a Payload.
There are a few types of Interface Definitions, including… 
Web Service Endpoint
Web Service Call
File Push
File Pull
Others
The Interface Definition Hub can be access from the Developer page nested under the Connect Hub. 
Interface Definitions can be organized in Groups for organization and maintainability.

## Slide 17

Types of Interfaces

Interface Definitions

Web Service
Endpoint / Call

File Service
Push / Pull

## Slide 18

Common Configuration

Interface Definitions

Linked Interface Definition
Typically, a reference to a parent interface definition

Massage Payload
The incoming payload definition.

Response Payload
The outgoing payload definition.

Complete Transaction in Success
Whether or not the interface transaction status is set to success after receiving payload and triggering post process actions.

Save Payload to Transaction
Whether or not payload message gets stored in transaction record.

Key
Unique identifier of the Interface Definition. This is important as it will be used to reference the Interface Definition during data processing

Name
Name of Interface Definition.  (non-programmatic)

Expiration Hours
How log transaction will persist in database.
Module Trigger Key
DMS module to trigger after transaction.
Process Definition Key
Workflow process to trigger after transaction.

## Slide 19

Web Service Endpoint Configuration

Interface Definitions

Route
Running location of the Web Service.
HTTP Method
Supported HTTP Methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE
Permission Set Key
Controls which user has permission to access the Web Service.
Permission Item Key
Controls which user has permission to access the Web Service.
Permission Action Key
Controls which user has permission to access the Web Service.

## Slide 20

Web Service Endpoint URL

Interface Definitions

Generated URL
By clicking on the ‘Copy Endpoint URL’ button on the interface configuration screen, you’ll be able to see the webservice URL.

## Slide 21

Web Service Call Configuration

Interface Definitions

URL
Running location of the webservice.
HTTP Method
Supported HTTP Methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE
Bearer Token
Token passed to an endpoint ensuring trusted connection.

## Slide 22

File Pull Configuration

Interface Definitions

Root Folder Path
Location where file service is looking for named folders below.
Login/Password
Security context for folder access
Source Folder Path
Location where file service is looking for new files.
Success Folder Path
Location where file service will move successfully processed files.
Failure Folder Path
Location where file service will move unsuccessfully processed files.
Search Pattern
File name pattern file service will use when looking for new files.
Max Files to Process
Number of files to process during a single pull. (0 = no limit)

## Slide 23

File Push Configuration

Interface Definitions

Target Path
Location where file service will place output file.
Login/Password
Security context for folder access
Target File Name
Name of file.

## Slide 24

Data Processing

## Slide 25

Options

Data Processing

DMS Module
Post Process

Workflow Process
Post Process

Script
In-Line

## Slide 26

Considerations

Data Processing

Why
Allows users to implement business logic in the interface. Common examples include the ability to merge data from a payload into a single field for mapping to TrakSYS entities.
Parameters Passed
When interfaces transactions trigger post process actions like DMS and Workflow. Some parameters are passed onto the next step as arguments, such as: Interface Definition ID, Interface Definition Key, and Interface Transaction ID.
Orchestration Options
	DMS
	Ideal for processing a single interface transaction.
	Workflow 
	Ideal for organizing events around an interface transaction.
	Plugin 
	Ideal for interacting with the interface transaction data before it’s passed downstream and/or for processing synchronously.

## Slide 27

Data Interface Example

## Slide 28

ERP Sending PO to TrakSYS via Web Service

Example

ERP / Middleware
TrakSYS Connect
TrakSYS DMS
TrakSYS Database
ERP Source calls exposed TrakSYS Connect Web Service and passes a large payload of PO/BOMs.
TrakSYS Connect Web Service receives the payload and saves it to Interface Transaction structures for later processing.
TrakSYS Connect Web Service ends the call from the ERP Source indicating that the payload was received.
TrakSYS Connect Web Service initiates an Async Trigger to fire a Data Management Service Module for processing the payload.
DMS Module accesses the saved payload for the specified Interface Transaction.
DMS Module processes the payload, validating business rules and creating the PO/BOM records in TrakSYS.
DMS Module may optionally trigger a separate TrakSYS Connect Web Service Call Interface to message ERP and indicate the Success or Failure of the PO processing.
TrakSYS Connect calls ERP hosted Web Service to pass async Success/Failure.

