## Slide 37

Logging

## Slide 38

Overview

Logging

Built in logging for every interface transaction.
Filter transactions to locate for monitoring and troubleshooting.
Transaction specific view and retry actions.
View transmitted payload for monitoring and troubleshooting.

## Slide 39

Transaction vs Log

Logging

tInterfaceTransaction
Top level information for the transaction.  One entry for every call or receive.
tInterfaceTransactionLog
Child information concerning a specific transaction.

## Slide 40

Content Pages

Logging

Interface Transaction Viewer
Standard log page specific to an Interface Definition
Payload Viewer
Standard view payload page. Note: this page is already referenced as part of the Interface Transaction Viewer page.

## Slide 41

Transaction Log Page Overview

Logging

Filters
Standard table filtering functions.
Transactions
List of interface transactions associated with the interface definition referencing in the page properties
Details
More information from the transaction when its row is clicked on.
Logs
A sub-log for the interface transaction where additional messages about the transaction can be stored and viewed.

## Slide 42

Transaction Log Page Configuration

Logging

Interface Definition ID
Interface for which the page with reference when displaying information.
Action Links
A set of up to 5 links that can be added to the transaction view table. These links will have access to transaction specific details and can use those as parameters when loading pages.

